# Performance & Zero-GC Rules

## No Allocations in update()
- STRICTLY FORBIDDEN to create new objects (`new Vec3()`, `new Color()`, `{}`, arrays) inside `update(dt)` or any 60fps handler.
- All temporary vectors, matrices and calculations MUST use pre-allocated scratch variables declared as class fields.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — scratch vars pre-allocated
private readonly _moveDir: Vec3 = new Vec3();
update(dt: number) {
    this._moveDir.set(x, 0, z);
}

// ❌ WRONG — allocation in update
update(dt: number) {
    const dir = new Vec3(x, 0, z); // GC spike!
}
```

## Object Pooling
- All repeating 3D objects (collectables, effects, projectiles) MUST be pre-created (prewarm) in `ObjectPool` during `BootState`.
- FORBIDDEN to call `instantiate()` / `destroy()` during active `GameplayState`.
- On collection: hide object and return to pool (`pool.release(item)`).

## Bundle Size Budget
- Final compiled single HTML build must NOT exceed **3 MB**.
- Textures: max 512×512, compressed PNG/JPG or Procedural Materials.
- 3D models: low-poly geometry only.
